# Per-Service SWC Compiler

Services that use NestJS class-based DI (constructor parameter inference) **must** use SWC as their dev compiler so that `emitDecoratorMetadata` is active at runtime. `tsx` (esbuild) does not support this flag.

## Canonical `.swcrc`

Place at `apps/<service>/.swcrc`:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/swcrc",
  "jsc": {
    "parser": { "syntax": "typescript", "decorators": true, "dynamicImport": true },
    "target": "es2023",
    "transform": {
      "legacyDecorator": true,
      "decoratorMetadata": true
    }
  },
  "module": { "type": "commonjs" },
  "sourceMaps": "inline"
}
```

`decoratorMetadata: true` is the critical flag — it emits `Reflect.metadata(...)` calls that NestJS reads to resolve constructor parameter types.

## Canonical `start:dev` Script

```json
"start:dev": "nodemon --watch src --ext ts,json --exec node -r @swc-node/register src/main.ts"
```

`@swc-node/register` is a Node.js `require` hook that compiles TypeScript on-the-fly using SWC, picking up `.swcrc` automatically.

## Required Per-Service devDependencies

```
pnpm --filter @ente-doctor/<service> add -D @swc/core @swc-node/register nodemon
```

Never install these at the workspace root.

## Production Build

Production continues to use `tsc` (`"build": "tsc -p tsconfig.json"`). SWC is dev-only.
